## Xkimm Xa Mali — System Design v1.0

### System Classification

```
Problem type:       Member-facing financial portal + automated payment management
Framework:          Next.js App Router (PWA-capable, SEO public pages, member portal)
Database:           PostgreSQL via Prisma (ACID compliance — non-negotiable for financial data)
Auth:               NextAuth.js + JWT HTTP-only cookies
Payment:            Netcash (SA-native DebiCheck debit order system)
SMS:                BulkSMS (leading SA provider, zero-rated gateway eligible)
Email:              Resend (transactional, developer-first)
Jobs/Cron:          Inngest (durable functions, event-driven, retryable)
Deployment:         Vercel (Next.js) + Neon (PostgreSQL) + Upstash (Redis)
```

**Why Netcash over PayFast:** Netcash is purpose-built for recurring debit order management in SA. It supports DebiCheck authenticated mandates, NAEDO, and batch collections. PayFast is optimized for once-off e-commerce payments.

**Why Inngest over Vercel Cron:** The notification + payment pipeline needs durable, retryable, event-driven jobs with full execution history. Inngest provides this natively. Vercel Cron fires and forgets.

